## 💡 Real-World Explanation

In an enterprise with 500 computers, if management requires all machines to lock their screens after 10 minutes of inactivity and block access to the Control Panel, manual configuration is impossible. 

SysAdmins use Group Policy to configure these settings once on the Domain Controller. When a user logs in, the client computer silently downloads the policy over the network and enforces the lockdown. If an employee tries to bypass it, Group Policy will re-apply the rule continuously in the background (by default, every 90 minutes).

