## ❓ Essential Interview Questions

Q1: What is the difference between Computer Configuration and User Configuration in a GPO?
A1: Computer Configuration applies to the machine during the boot process (before login) and affects all users on that machine. User Configuration applies at the time of login and follows the specific user regardless of what machine they sit at.

Q2: If a user tells you their new Group Policy settings haven't applied yet, what command can they run on their PC to force the update?
A2: `gpupdate /force`

Q3: What does the command `gpmc.msc` do?
A3: It opens the Group Policy Management Console.